WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.236
-It's been almost two weeks

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.171
since the horrific shootings
in Parkland, Florida,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.506
and the Never Again Movement
started by students

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:10.076
at Stoneman Douglas High School
continues to intensify,

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:13.213
putting more and more pressure
on Republicans and the NRA.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.381
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.916 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.719
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.422
-President Trump's approval
ratings have fallen back down

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:25.258
to historically low levels
amid an avalanche of scandal

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.525
and chaos in his administration.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.961
And yet, on Friday,

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.764
Trump went to the Conservative
Political Action Conference

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:34.600
and made this outlandish claim
about all the promises he's made

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.968
that he supposedly kept.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:39.238
-Remember this, we've gotten --
you know,

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.207
somebody got on television
recently and they said,

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.176
"Actually this is the first time
I can remember,

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.244
Trump made campaign promises.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.615
He may be the only person
that actually fulfilled

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.317
more promises than he made."
I think that's true.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.086
-Oh, my God,
what is he talking about?

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.254
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.389
Trump is so garbled,
his speeches are becoming

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.790
logical paradoxes.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.160
[ As Trump ] "I fulfill promises
I haven't even made.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.895
I married a woman I haven't met.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.397
And I made a rock so heavy,
I can't lift it."

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.932
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.200
[ Normal voice ] Trump claims
he heard someone on television

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.869
make that claim,
and he's just repeating it.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.838
And I think he must have
gotten it from this guy

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.173
a few weeks ago.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.773
-I was there four months.
You know this, Paul.

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:18.711
And they were saying,
"He didn't fulfill a promise."

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:23.316
But now we fulfilled far more
promises than we promised.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.818
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:29.856
-Does Trump think that the Trump
on TV is a different guy?

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.357
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.958
[ As Trump ]
"He's back. He's on TV again.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:35.261
Ohh. I like the cut of his jib.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.096
I'm going to copy his haircut."

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.364
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.999
[ Normal voice ] Of course,
the immediate crisis

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.901
facing Trump and the rest
of the government right now

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.836
is our country's epidemic
of gun violence.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.771
The national conversation
over gun safety

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.441
has only intensified in the days
since the Parkland shooting.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.775
And people are demanding action.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.211
And in response
to those demands,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.813
Trump has spent the last week
or so rambling nonsensically

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.482
about his truly deranged idea
to arm teachers.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.651
And today he took that rambling
one step further,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.687
insisting that he personally
would have run into the school

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:03.990
to confront the shooter
whether he was armed or not.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.057
-You know, I really believe --

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.392
you don't know
until you're tested,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.827
but I think, I really believe

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.229
I'd run in there even if
I didn't have a weapon.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.031
-Nothing about that is
believable.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.599
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:15.868
Forget running into a school
to confront a shooter.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.004
I don't believe you'd
run anywhere, period.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:21.174
You can't even be bothered to
walk down a flight of stairs.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.142
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.511
Then, again, I said before
that I didn't think he'd run,

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:27.246
and, man, did I get burned.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.914
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:32.218
There's really nothing worse
than a fake tough guy.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.819
Trump lives in a fantasy world

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:35.522
where he's some sort
of action movie star

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.590
who'd rush into danger
and save the day.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.093
I'm sorry, but you're
not exactly Liam Neeson.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.727
If you've been in the movie,
"Taken,"

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.830 line:0%
they would have had
to change the name.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:48.834 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.504
[ As Trump ]
"All right. So you have her?

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.006
Okay. Okay.

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.475
Thanks for the call."

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.943
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.277
[ Normal voice ]
But it kept getting worse,

00:02:58.277 --> 00:02:59.712
because Trump
lashed out at the media

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.847
accurately describing his plan
to arm teachers

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:03.482
as a plan to arm teachers,

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.818
insisting that he would
only give guns to teachers

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.287
who knew how to use them.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.621
-When the press covered it,
the headline was,

00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:11.390
"Trump wants all teachers

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.658
to have guns.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.427
Trump wants teachers
to have guns."

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.795
I don't want teachers
to have guns.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.664
I want highly trained people

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:20.700
that have a natural talent,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.401
like hitting a baseball

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.370
or hitting a golf ball
or putting.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.771
How come some people always make

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:28.641
the four footer and some people

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.944
under pressure can't even
take their club back?

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.411
Right?

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:35.315
-Well, even when
he's laying out his plan

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.882
to prevent school shootings,

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:40.018
he can't hide how much
he'd rather be playing golf.

00:03:40.018 --> 00:03:43.923
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:48.728
Also, the only people
who ask how come some people

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.496
always make the four footer
are the people

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.031
who never make the four footer.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.133
When Trump putts,
I bet he makes Eric

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.668
lie down on the green to try
and blow his ball into the hole.

00:03:56.668 --> 00:03:57.836
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.836 --> 00:04:00.806
[ As Eric ] "Father,
I'm running out of air!"

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.007
[ Normal voice ]
Of course, the only reason

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:03.476
we're still talking about
the issue of gun violence

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.744
is because of the students
at Stoneman Douglas High School

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:07.013
who have demanded action

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.614
and sparked a national movement
for gun reform.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.016
Their passionate calls
for action have disrupted

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:12.618
the usual routine
that seems to unfold

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.019
after every mass shooting.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:16.856
And for that, they've been
subjected to deranged attacks

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.123
on everything from
their maturity

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:19.691
to their credibility
to their tone.

00:04:19.691 --> 00:04:21.627
Like Stoneman Douglas student
Sarah Chadwick,

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.863
who was scolded by conservatives
when she tweeted,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:27.132
"We should change the names
of AR-15s to 'Marco Rubio'

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:28.801
because they are so easy
to buy."

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.169
[ Audience "ohhs" and cheers ]

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.805
Daaaamn.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.640
Damn.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.710
That is a white-hot burn.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.611
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.779
There's only one thing to do

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:43.149
when you get burned that hard,
Marco.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:46.586
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, drink up!

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.988
After that tweet,
Fox News host Laura Ingraham

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.990
quoted Chadwick's line
on Twitter and added,

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.192
"How teens speak to
and about adults,"

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:56.328
calling her Stoneman Douglas
sophomore Sarah Chadwick.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:58.430
Which prompted this response
from Chadwick --

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.598
"I'm a junior."

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:02.235
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:05.238
Laura Ingraham,
what is wrong with you?!

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.707
Don't go after teenagers
on social media.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.509
You saw what happened
to Marco Rubio.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.676
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:13.012
So in short, Marco Rubio
might be easy to buy,

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.914
but Laura Ingraham
is easy to own.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.682
[ Audience "ohhs", laughs ]

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:18.184
"Ohhhh."

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.886
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:22.755
And then there are those who
have spent the last two weeks

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.557
lecturing students
on their maturity

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.892
and their qualifications
for talking about gun reform

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.894
and claiming their movement
is somehow being hijacked

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.229
by left-wing groups.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.999
-The media's focused more
on a teenager's expertise

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.768
in supply-side control measures
for guns,

00:05:36.768 --> 00:05:38.537
which, Tucker, let's be candid.

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.105
They probably have not studied

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:42.374
a very complicated,
layered issue.

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:44.776
-Their sorrow can very easily

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:47.112
be hijacked by left-wing groups

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:49.082
who have an agenda.
-But do you think it has been?

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.649
-Well, let's ask ourselves,

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.584
do we really think that --

00:05:52.584 --> 00:05:53.785
and I say this sincerely.

00:05:53.785 --> 00:05:56.255
Do we really think 17-year-olds

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.690
on their own are going to plan

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.391
a nationwide rally?

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:01.327
-You don't think 17-year-olds

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.195
can plan a rally?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:05.864
17-year-olds know
how to plan things.

00:06:05.864 --> 00:06:08.267
When you're 17, you're too young
to do most things,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.635
so you have to find ways
around it.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:12.437
You got to get fake I.D.s,
coordinate alibis,

00:06:12.437 --> 00:06:14.640
figure out how to make
a bong out of an apple,

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.708
an inhaler, and a straw.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:18.377
You got to bring Scope with you

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:20.246
so you can wash away
the smell of alcohol.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.914
But then your parents smell
a ton of Scope,

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.315
and they knew you were drinking.

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:24.416
But they're also
a little impressed

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:25.484
you remembered to bring Scope.

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.053
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:29.155
The attacks on these students
are clear evidence

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.289
that the movement is working.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:31.724
The NRA and their supporters
are scared.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.325
And now the NRA and their allies

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:35.494
are resorting to increasingly
ludicrous suggestions

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:37.696
for how to deal with
gun violence in schools.

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.265
Trump, for example, spent
the weekend repeating

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:42.000
his deranged idea
for giving guns to teachers

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.069
in his CPAC speech,
and then again

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.504
in the interview with Fox News.

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:48.040
-We would have had some

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.742
great teachers that were

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.510
gun adept, meaning, you know,

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.846
really understood weaponry
and guns.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:56.015
And if they had
concealed permits,

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.217
you wouldn't have this problem
today.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:01.186
-This is one of the worst things
about having Trump as president.

00:07:01.186 --> 00:07:04.123
Every time he goes on TV
and blurts the dumbest things

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:05.957
in the world, the rest of us
have to debate it

00:07:05.957 --> 00:07:07.393
like it's a real idea.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.361
He says, "Hey,
I think we should take

00:07:09.361 --> 00:07:10.696
incredibly stressed out people

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.832
who make $30,000 a year
and give them guns."

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:14.633
And then Wolf Blitzer
has to stand there and go,

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:16.968
"[Bleep]
Well, let's ask the panel.

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:19.271
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:21.774
He said it.
So now I got to ask you all.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:26.645
You have to give me answers
like it's a real thing."

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:29.215
And there's no evidence that
anywhere close to 10% to 20%

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:31.483
of teachers have firearms
training, as Trump claims.

00:07:31.483 --> 00:07:32.552
Nor is there any evidence

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:34.486
it would actually prevent
school shootings.

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:36.655
Second, there's the question
of how teachers, themselves,

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:37.956
feel about this idea.

00:07:37.956 --> 00:07:39.759
And in the days
since Trump floated it,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:40.793
the response from teachers,

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:42.561
including those from
Stoneman Douglas,

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:44.229
have been a resounding
"No thanks."

00:07:44.229 --> 00:07:46.131
-You heard the President today.

00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:48.367
He in effect wants people like

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.802
you to be on the front lines,

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.404
to be armed.

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:53.538
If you have the aptitude for it,

00:07:53.538 --> 00:07:55.240
"aptitude," as he described it.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.077
Is that a good idea?

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:01.347
-No. I have no desire to

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:02.814
own a gun, carry a gun,

00:08:02.814 --> 00:08:04.383
shoot a gun, touch a gun.

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:05.585
And the President said that

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.152
those of us who would be willing

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:08.253
to be armed would get

00:08:08.253 --> 00:08:09.755
some kind of a bonus.

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.590
I'm not even given adequate

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:12.891
money to buy supplies

00:08:12.891 --> 00:08:14.193
for my classroom.

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.595
But now if I choose to carry
a gun,

00:08:16.595 --> 00:08:18.364
a gun will be provided for me,

00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:20.366
and I will be given a bonus?

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.835
-Now, I know we didn't
get to them in the clip.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:26.571
But just in case you're curious,
the guy on the right's pro-gun.

00:08:26.571 --> 00:08:28.908
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:33.913
I know.

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:36.148
I know you're all watching
the clip.

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:37.416
You're like, "Yeah.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.418
What's the guy in the super
clean cowboy hat think?"

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:40.352
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.352 --> 00:08:42.654
Very pro-gun. [ Chuckles ]

00:08:42.654 --> 00:08:44.756
But seriously,
the teacher's right.

00:08:44.756 --> 00:08:46.892
Teachers need supplies,
not guns.

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:49.762
The only guns that should be
in schools are glue guns.

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:51.763
And they should be used
the way all students use them,

00:08:51.763 --> 00:08:53.966
to glue the shop teacher's butt
to his chair.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:57.336
And when they're not calling
for more guns in schools,

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.671
gun supporters are complaining
that it's actually video games

00:08:59.671 --> 00:09:01.307
and movies that are causing
violence,

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.675
as Trump did last week.

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.344
-I'm hearing more and more
people say the level of violence

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:10.048
on video games is really shaping
young people's thoughts.

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:13.019
And then you go the further
step, and that's the movies.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.854
You see these movies,
they're so violent.

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:20.058
And yet, a kid is able to see
the movie if sex isn't involved.

00:09:20.058 --> 00:09:21.560
But killing is involved,

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.864
and maybe they have to put
a rating system for that.

00:09:24.864 --> 00:09:28.434
-Does Trump not know that movies
already have a rating system?

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:31.003
I love how he's always
trying to suggest things

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:32.237
that already exist.

00:09:32.237 --> 00:09:33.873
[ As Trump ] "Movies should have
a rating system,

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:36.041
and on top of that,
you should have to buy a ticket.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:38.510
I think we can all agree.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.145
And they should have
a concession stand

00:09:40.145 --> 00:09:44.216
where they sell some sort of
snack made from popped corn.

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:45.584
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.553
You could call it corn pop."

00:09:47.553 --> 00:09:48.821
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.122
[ Normal voice ] But you
know what -- Trump is right.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:51.690
People are way too influenced
by movies.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.592
Just take this guy
as an example.

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:55.594
-In fact, I have a license
to carry in New York.

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:57.329
Can you believe that?
Nobody knows that.

00:09:57.329 --> 00:09:58.697
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:58.697 --> 00:10:00.966
What was the famous movie,
remember?

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:02.101
[ Crowd shouting suggestions ]

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:04.670
No. Remember?

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.471
Where he went around
and he sort of --

00:10:06.471 --> 00:10:10.376
after his wife was hurt so badly
and killed?

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:12.043
What?

00:10:12.043 --> 00:10:15.648
Charles Bronson, right?
The late, great Charles Bronson.

00:10:15.648 --> 00:10:17.850
Name of the movie? Come on.
[ Crowd shouting suggestions ]

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.319
"Death Wish." Remember that?

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:22.187
"Oh, we're going to
cut you up, sir.

00:10:22.187 --> 00:10:24.289
We're going to cut you up.
Oh, oh, oh."

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.292
Bing. One of the great movies.

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:29.028
But could you imagine
with Trump, somebody says,

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:31.931
"Oh, all these big monsters
aren't around.

00:10:31.931 --> 00:10:34.733
It's easy pickings, and then --"
P-ching!

00:10:34.733 --> 00:10:38.471
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:41.607
-And you think 17-year-olds

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:44.042
are too immature
to discuss gun control?

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:47.312
He's literally making
gun sound effects.

00:10:47.312 --> 00:10:48.914
And the wrong ones --

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:50.849
[ As Trump ] Bink, boink,
woop, woop, woop, woop, woop!

00:10:50.849 --> 00:10:53.885
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:53.885 --> 00:10:58.524
Huh?

00:10:58.524 --> 00:11:00.626
[ Normal voice ] Commentators
on the right have spent the days

00:11:00.626 --> 00:11:02.761
since the Parkland shooting
insisting that teenagers

00:11:02.761 --> 00:11:04.629
are somehow too immature
to comment on the issue

00:11:04.629 --> 00:11:06.398
like gun reform,
when in reality,

00:11:06.398 --> 00:11:08.333
the only people who sound like
children are the ones

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:10.602
using phrases like "good guys"
and "bad guys"

00:11:10.602 --> 00:11:13.205
and pretending that all you need
to do to stop a school shooting

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:15.341
is have someone there
to run in and go --

00:11:15.341 --> 00:11:16.574
-Bink.

00:11:16.574 --> 00:11:17.576
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:17.576 --> 00:11:18.844
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:18.844 --> 00:11:20.279 line:0%
♪♪

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:22.415
[ Cheers and applause ]

